WEBVTT

NOTE Draft cue timing follows measured scene audio and word count. Review spoken word alignment before publication.

00:00:00.000 --> 00:00:05.765
Welcome to Resgrid Academy. In this lesson, we will keep deployment activity and

00:00:05.765 --> 00:00:11.530
cost evidence together. Extended mutual-aid work needs clear personnel, apparatus, dates, and cost

00:00:11.530 --> 00:00:17.295
records that can be reviewed after demobilization. We will explain the features, the

00:00:17.295 --> 00:00:21.730
setup decisions, and a practical way to check the result.

00:00:22.330 --> 00:00:28.166
A strike-team deployment is recorded with its personnel, apparatus and dates. Keep deployment

00:00:28.166 --> 00:00:34.003
records and cost documentation together for review and reimbursement. The examples in this

00:00:34.003 --> 00:00:39.390
series use a fictional department and are teaching scenarios, not default settings.

00:00:39.990 --> 00:00:46.872
Deployment Finance. Deployment records and Deployment Finance. Record your next deployment with its

00:00:46.872 --> 00:00:48.460
personnel and apparatus.

00:00:49.060 --> 00:00:55.268
New Deployment. Start a deployment record. Useful when your members deploy to incidents

00:00:55.268 --> 00:00:56.700
outside your jurisdiction.

00:00:57.300 --> 00:01:03.168
Deployment From External Order. Create a deployment from a mutual-aid resource order. Useful

00:01:03.168 --> 00:01:07.230
when your members deploy to incidents outside your jurisdiction.

00:01:07.830 --> 00:01:14.296
Resource orders describe requested resources and the fills departments offer or accept. Review

00:01:14.296 --> 00:01:20.761
ordering settings and participating departments. Create a fictional request, offer a fill, and

00:01:20.761 --> 00:01:27.227
review acceptance. Reconcile requested quantities, accepted fills, and the remaining resource need. Confirm

00:01:27.227 --> 00:01:32.200
availability in the demo department before recording the live workflow.

00:01:32.800 --> 00:01:38.814
An external order records the department fills and their mobilization, release, and actual

00:01:38.814 --> 00:01:44.827
return home. Enter an approved sample external order, link its deployment, record the

00:01:44.827 --> 00:01:50.841
fill transitions, and complete closeout. Review dates and resource identity. This workspace records

00:01:50.841 --> 00:01:56.854
manual entry and artifact snapshots; it is not an external ordering connector. Confirm

00:01:56.854 --> 00:02:01.480
availability in the demo department before recording the live workflow.

00:02:02.080 --> 00:02:08.239
Read-only deployment reports bring time entries, supporting artifacts, and export outputs together. Open

00:02:08.239 --> 00:02:14.399
a recorded demo deployment and review its time report, summary, and available exports.

00:02:14.399 --> 00:02:20.558
Reconcile each time entry with the roster and recorded dates before finance review.

00:02:20.558 --> 00:02:25.770
Confirm availability in the demo department before recording the live workflow.

00:02:26.370 --> 00:02:32.763
For the training scenario, work in this order. Step 1. Create a deployment

00:02:32.763 --> 00:02:39.156
or start from an external resource order. Step 2. Identify the assigned personnel,

00:02:39.156 --> 00:02:45.548
apparatus, and operational dates. Step 3. Record deployment activity and finance documentation for

00:02:45.548 --> 00:02:46.040
review.

00:02:46.640 --> 00:02:52.490
Now verify the result. Reconcile the deployment resources and dates with supporting records.

00:02:52.490 --> 00:02:58.340
Review any daily time and cost documentation required by the workflow. A common

00:02:58.340 --> 00:03:04.190
problem to watch for: Deployment Finance is separate from the Business Operations add-on.

00:03:04.190 --> 00:03:07.340
A prepared record does not guarantee reimbursement.

00:03:07.940 --> 00:03:13.146
Your practice task is simple. Record a two-day demo strike-team deployment and reconcile

00:03:13.146 --> 00:03:18.351
the participating people and units with the supporting documents. Record the result, who

00:03:18.351 --> 00:03:23.557
owns the follow-up, and when it should be reviewed. Use the linked feature

00:03:23.557 --> 00:03:26.360
scripts for the detailed screen recording plan.

